WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.434
-Donald Trump is sharpening

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.367
his attacks against one
of his likely opponents

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:07.000
for the GOP nomination,
Florida Governor Ron DeSantis,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.868
even as prosecutors
in New York indicate

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:11.300
that they are closer than ever
to indicting Trump

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.033
and members
of a Georgia grand jury

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:15.167
say their investigation
of Trump could be massive.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.601
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:22.067
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:25.000
Trump and DeSantis have both
been hitting the campaign trail,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.234
even though DeSantis has not

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:27.667
officially announced
that he's running yet.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:28.834
But I mean,
you can tell he's running.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.701
For one thing,
he seems to be wearing suits

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:31.901
that actually fit him, now,

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:34.000
instead of whatever the hell's
going on here.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.801
He looks like he's cheating
in a chess tournament.

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.734
Look, I get it.
We've all been there.

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:42.834
You got a formal event,
you forget to buy a suit,

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.534
you rifle through your closet
at the last minute

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:46.634
and you find an old jacket
that doesn't fit anymore

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:49.133
and you end up looking like
a cat standing on its hind legs.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:53.667
Been there.

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:55.300
But DeSantis gearing up
for a run

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.000
also means he's attracted
the bloodshot Eye of Sauron,

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.267
[ Laughter ]
his main rival, Donald Trump,
who's been attacking DeSantis

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:03.701
on the campaign trail
and elsewhere.

00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:06.334
In fact, Trump posted a pretty
remarkable video this week,

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:08.901
where he basically said
DeSantis was a failure

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.834
and the only reason
people like Florida

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:12.133
is because it's sunny there.

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:14.267
-For those of you
that didn't notice,

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:18.667
Florida was doing great long
before Ron DeSanctis got there.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:22.567
[ Laughter ]
People are fleeing from New York
to Florida, and other places,

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:25.934
because of high taxes
and out of control crime.

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:27.267
It's really bad.

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.534
[ Laughter ]
Not because of the governor --

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:32.868
thank you, Mr. President,
for doing that --

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:34.701
but it's not
because of the governor.

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:36.534
Florida was doing fantastically.

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:38.100
You had a governor
named Rick Scott

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.868
who did a very good job.

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.400
Even Charlie Crist, a Democrat,
did a good job,

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.167
and he had very good numbers.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:47.133
Sunshine and ocean
are very alluring.

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:51.701
-He sounds like a '60s radical,

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:54.300
explaining how two women
tricked him into joining a cult.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.634
[ Laughter ]
[ Hippie voice ] Sunshine --

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:58.734
Sunshine and Ocean
were very alluring, man.

00:01:58.734 --> 00:01:59.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:02.200
They told me my chakra's
aligned with theirs.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.434
Next thing I knew,
my bank account was empty

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:06.634
and I was scrubbing
the maharishi's toilet.

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:10.901
[ Laughter ]
Still, man, I wouldn't trade
those times for anything.

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:13.067
I can't believe I'm saying this,
but I agree with Donald Trump.

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:14.968
Everything people like
about Florida

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.734
was in place
before Ron DeSantis.

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:18.868
He didn't do something magical
and suddenly convince people

00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:20.267
they should move
to a warmer climate,

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:22.834
with beaches, golf courses,
theme parks, low taxes,

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:23.934
alligators on meth.

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:25.968
[ Laughter ]
If you think people living

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:27.033
in New York were saying,

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:28.400
"There's too many books
around here.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.968
I want to go to a state
where there's less to read."

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:32.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:34.033
But that video is such
a funny preview

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:36.434
of how Trump is going to tear
into all of his opponents.

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:39.067
He's already so mad at DeSantis,
he's praising

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:41.901
the former governor of Florida
Charlie Crist

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:43.634
[ Laughter ]
for doing a better job
than DeSantis.

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.467
Soon, Trump's going to be
so desperate to attack

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.834
his fellow Republicans,
he's going to endorse Obama.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.234
[ Laughter ]
[ As Trump ] You know,

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:51.234
you know where else has sunshine
and ocean?

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:53.767
[ Laughter ]
Hawaii, home to my good friend
Barack Obama.

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:55.501
He was born there.

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:56.801
[ Laughter ]
He was born in Hawaii.

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.367
He has the birth certificate
and every-- I've seen it.

00:02:58.367 --> 00:02:59.934
Beautiful birth certificate,
beautiful.

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:01.367
[ Laughter and applause ]
Gold leaf.

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:02.634
Held it in my hands.

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:04.734
Obama -- great man, great man.

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:07.334
Good at basketball.
He tried to teach poor Ron how

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:10.300
to shoot a three-pointer,
but Ron couldn't

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.400
raise his arms above his head.
So sad.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:15.467
So sad.

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:17.634
There's plenty more
to attack DeSantis on

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:21.367
because, as we've said before,
DeSantis is a weird guy,

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:24.334
but not as weird as Trump,
which is his main problem.

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:27.167
If you're a GOP voter who likes
weird, Trump's your guy.

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:29.267
But if you're normal --
if you like normal,

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:31.033
DeSantis is a little too weird.

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:34.634
He stands weird. He wears those
little, weird white boots.

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:36.300
[ Laughter ]
And now --

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.868
And now there's this new story
about his weird eating habits.

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:50.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:01.300
[ Laughter and ohhs ]

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.701
You ate pudding
with your fingers?

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:04.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:06.734
That's not very DeSanitary.

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:08.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:11.567
You don't get to use
your fingers to eat pudding!

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:12.901
Here are the rules.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:16.000
If you have pudding,
but you don't have a spoon,

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.534
then you
don't have pudding.

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:19.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.434
I've never thought
I'd say this about anyone,

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:23.567
but you should eat
more like Donald Trump.

00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:24.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:25.801
If you were in a plane next
to a guy

00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:27.667
who was finger-blasting
Swiss Miss

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.467
[ Laughter ]
and asked to move

00:04:29.467 --> 00:04:32.167
and the flight attendant said,
"The only open seat's next

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:35.534
to a dude eating KFC
with a knife and fork,"

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:37.667
you'd say, "Yeah, I guess,
in this case,

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.334
it beats the pudding dude."

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:42.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.267
So, there's a lot of material
for Trump to work with.

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:47.467
The only thing Trump hasn't
nailed down yet is the nickname.

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:49.734
I mean, I took Ron DeSanitary,
so that one's gone.

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:51.634
Sorry, dude.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:54.067
Trump's been calling him
Ron DeSanctimonious,

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:56.634
which doesn't exactly roll right
off the tongue,

00:04:56.634 --> 00:04:58.467
so, then he shortens it.

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:01.067
He shortens DeSanctimonious
to make it easier to say.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:05.100
-Florida was doing great long
before Ron DeSanctis got there.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.968
[ Laughter ]
So just remember,
Florida was doing really well

00:05:07.968 --> 00:05:10.667
long before Ron DeSanctis
got there.

00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:13.267
-So, he shortened Sanctimonious
to Sanctis.

00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:14.634
Makes total sense.

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:16.968
Smart people always shorten
long words like that.

00:05:16.968 --> 00:05:18.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:20.501
I remember when I got
my appendix looked at,

00:05:20.501 --> 00:05:21.667
the doctor came in and said,

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:22.901
"Alright, looks like
we're going to have to do

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:24.367
a little appendy,
but don't worry.

00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:26.734
[ Laughter ]
If anything happens,
we'll just shock you

00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:27.734
with defibbies."

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:29.100
[ Laughter ]
I don't know

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.167
if he was a good doctor or not

00:05:30.167 --> 00:05:31.767
because I didn't stay!

00:05:31.767 --> 00:05:33.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:34.868
So, Trump's decided to go
after DeSantis

00:05:34.868 --> 00:05:36.634
before DeSantis even gets
in the race

00:05:36.634 --> 00:05:38.300
and the most important
media organization

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.901
in the conservative movement,
Fox News, seems torn about it.

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:42.734
On the one hand, you have hosts,
like Brian Kilmeade,

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:44.100
who are cozying up to DeSantis,

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.300
but also seem impressed
by what they claim

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.434
is Trump's ability
to stay on message

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:49.901
after a run of bad press.

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:52.033
-He also is on a bit of a roll

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:54.367
since he went and visited
East Palestine,

00:05:54.367 --> 00:05:56.934
stopped having lunch
with white supremacists,

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:59.100
and has got
a very disciplined message.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.801
-I can't argue with the logic.

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:02.167
It's like saying,
"Hannibal Lecter

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:05.033
has been looking svelte
since he stopped eating people."

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:06.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:08.167
Also, I love
that they're still waiting,

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.000
all these years later,
for a more disciplined

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.267
Donald Trump
to magically appear.

00:06:11.267 --> 00:06:13.634
The man's 76. 76-year-olds
don't suddenly change,

00:06:13.634 --> 00:06:15.100
unless they start taking Cialis.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.334
[ Laughter ]
You know, after he started
taking Cialis,

00:06:18.334 --> 00:06:20.501
Grandpa bought a fedora
and joined a band.

00:06:20.501 --> 00:06:22.033
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.033 --> 00:06:24.601
But, of course, the big question
looming over the GOP primary is

00:06:24.601 --> 00:06:25.834
whether Trump will get indicted.

00:06:25.834 --> 00:06:27.467
He's facing
multiple investigations

00:06:27.467 --> 00:06:29.033
in various jurisdictions,
at this point,

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:30.868
including state
and federal investigations

00:06:30.868 --> 00:06:33.133
of his attempt to overturn
the 2020 election.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:35.367
And I'm as tired as anyone

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:36.801
of hearing the probe
is intensifying

00:06:36.801 --> 00:06:38.434
and the walls
are closing in on Trump.

00:06:38.434 --> 00:06:40.267
It's like waiting around
for Sam and Diane

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:41.501
to finally kiss or, you know,

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:43.367
a better reference,
for people under 50.

00:06:43.367 --> 00:06:46.868
[ Laughter ]
But in New York,
prosecutors are looking

00:06:46.868 --> 00:06:49.534
into Trump's hush money payments
from 2016

00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:52.534
and that case might be the
closest to an actual indictment.

00:06:52.534 --> 00:06:54.300
-Donald Trump's former attorney
Michael Cohen

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.934
making his second
appearance tomorrow

00:06:55.934 --> 00:06:57.467
before a New York grand jury.

00:06:57.467 --> 00:06:58.667
He's the key witness in a case

00:06:58.667 --> 00:07:00.267
investigating
a hush money payment

00:07:00.267 --> 00:07:03.100
to adult film star
Stormy Daniels,

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:06.167
that payment made just days
before the 2016 election.

00:07:06.167 --> 00:07:07.968
Prosecutors handling the case
are signaling

00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:10.701
that a criminal indictment
for Trump could be coming soon.

00:07:10.701 --> 00:07:11.968
-Man, it would be wild

00:07:11.968 --> 00:07:13.934
if that's the thing
that brought Trump down.

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:15.367
The guy was impeached twice,

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:16.834
colluded with one
foreign country,

00:07:16.834 --> 00:07:18.734
tried to extort another country
to interfere

00:07:18.734 --> 00:07:20.667
in a presidential election
on his behalf,

00:07:20.667 --> 00:07:22.767
and then fomented a violent coup
to stay in power,

00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:24.033
but the thing that
could finally sink him

00:07:24.033 --> 00:07:25.467
is paying off a porn star

00:07:25.467 --> 00:07:27.467
not to tell everyone
about his weird penis,

00:07:27.467 --> 00:07:29.934
when everyone already assumed
it looked weird.

00:07:29.934 --> 00:07:31.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:31.234 --> 00:07:33.734
Talk about throwing bad money
after good.

00:07:33.734 --> 00:07:35.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:35.167 --> 00:07:37.334
But Trump apparently has a new
lawyer to handle this case,

00:07:37.334 --> 00:07:39.968
a guy whose real name is
Joe Tacopina.

00:07:39.968 --> 00:07:41.100
I did not make that up.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.534
I certainly would never use it
as a joke.

00:07:42.534 --> 00:07:45.501
Like if someone asked me what
Stormy Daniels said about Trump,

00:07:45.501 --> 00:07:47.501
I would never say,
"He's got a little Tacopina."

00:07:47.501 --> 00:07:48.601
I wouldn't do that.

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:50.734 --> 00:07:52.934
But Tacopina went
on MSNBC this week

00:07:52.934 --> 00:07:54.534
to defend Trump's lie
that he didn't know

00:07:54.534 --> 00:07:56.234
about the hush payment
with Stormy Daniels

00:07:56.234 --> 00:07:57.434
and the interview
got contentious.

00:07:57.434 --> 00:08:00.133
-One of the top trial attorneys
out of New York,

00:08:00.133 --> 00:08:03.067
Joe Tacopina,
is defending Donald Trump

00:08:03.067 --> 00:08:05.968
and our guests right now,
live on "The Beat," is...

00:08:05.968 --> 00:08:08.601
Trump defense lawyer
Joe Tacopina.

00:08:08.601 --> 00:08:09.767
[ Laughter ]
If all of what you say

00:08:09.767 --> 00:08:11.167
is true...
-It is.

00:08:11.167 --> 00:08:12.467
[ Laughter ]
-...then why was Trump hiding it

00:08:12.467 --> 00:08:13.868
and lying about it at the time?

00:08:13.868 --> 00:08:15.367
And I'll play that
for your response.

00:08:15.367 --> 00:08:16.667
-Mm-hmm.
-He lied about it.

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:17.567
We all know that. Take a look.
-When you say he lied --

00:08:17.567 --> 00:08:18.534
-Take a look.
-Let's see.

00:08:19.667 --> 00:08:20.934
-Mr. President, did...

00:08:36.834 --> 00:08:38.567
-Ari, that is --

00:08:38.567 --> 00:08:40.067
if that's what you're going
to consider a lie --

00:08:40.067 --> 00:08:41.901
A lie, to me,
Is something material,

00:08:41.901 --> 00:08:44.334
under oath, in a procedural.
-I didn't say perjury.

00:08:44.334 --> 00:08:46.234
I said a lie.
-Yeah, but that's not a lie.

00:08:46.234 --> 00:08:47.834
That's called --
-That's not a lie?

00:08:47.834 --> 00:08:49.067
-Here's why it's not a lie.

00:08:49.067 --> 00:08:50.701
-That's not a lie?
-Here's why it's not a lie.

00:08:50.701 --> 00:08:51.868
Could you put your paper --
-"Did you know about this?

00:08:51.868 --> 00:08:53.567
-Put the paper down.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.567 --> 00:08:54.734
Let me answer.
-Did you know about this?"

00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:56.367
"No, I don't."
-We don't need that.

00:08:56.367 --> 00:08:58.067
-[ As Tacopina ]
Hey, oh, what's with the paper?

00:08:58.067 --> 00:09:00.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:00.133 --> 00:09:01.667
Hey!
I thought we were friends.

00:09:01.667 --> 00:09:02.934
Come on, we don't need that.

00:09:02.934 --> 00:09:04.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.334
You take out paper,
I got to take out scissors.

00:09:06.334 --> 00:09:07.601
Next thing you know,

00:09:07.601 --> 00:09:09.634
you're eating your pudding
with only two fingers.

00:09:09.634 --> 00:09:12.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:12.534 --> 00:09:14.701
As we mentioned, there are
other investigations of Trump,

00:09:14.701 --> 00:09:15.767
including one in Georgia,

00:09:15.767 --> 00:09:17.067
where prosecutors
are investigating

00:09:17.067 --> 00:09:18.868
Trump's attempt to interfere
in the vote count

00:09:18.868 --> 00:09:20.400
and are weighing whether
to bring charges.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.200
The Atlanta Journal-Constitution
recently spoke

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.767
to anonymous members
of the grand jury,

00:09:24.767 --> 00:09:26.667
who said the findings
were potentially explosive.

00:09:26.667 --> 00:09:27.334
One juror said...

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.033
And another said...

00:09:38.701 --> 00:09:40.467
That is quite the tease.

00:09:40.467 --> 00:09:42.033
When I read that,
I was so shocked,

00:09:42.033 --> 00:09:44.467
I stood up straight like
Ron DeSantis.

00:09:44.467 --> 00:09:47.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:47.801 --> 00:09:50.634
Now, if all that's true,
then I personally feel like

00:09:50.634 --> 00:09:53.100
it might be better
to charge the guy

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.968
who fomented a violent coup
to overthrow American democracy

00:09:55.968 --> 00:09:58.567
with coup stuff, first,
instead of the hush money stuff.

00:09:58.567 --> 00:09:59.834
I'm not saying Trump shouldn't

00:09:59.834 --> 00:10:01.567
face legal consequences
in that case, too.

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:03.033
I just think it might be better
for democracy

00:10:03.033 --> 00:10:04.968
if we held Trump accountable
for the coup,

00:10:04.968 --> 00:10:06.601
than if we charged him
for paying someone not

00:10:06.601 --> 00:10:07.467
to talk about his little...

00:10:07.467 --> 00:10:08.400
-Tacopina.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:10.067
[ Laughter and applause ]
-This

00:10:10.067 --> 00:10:11.200
has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:14.968
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

